  {
   "id": 242792,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/5adb519536436bd2.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Bert Tolkamp, et al./SAC)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The table shows feed conversion ratios (FCR) for different farm animals. FCR is calculated by dividing the amount of feed given to the animal by the animal's edible weight. \"Broiler\" chickens are chicken raised for their meat.</p>\n<p>You are the owner of a farm who wants to raise livestock for meat. You want the livestock to have efficient FCR, but do not want to raise birds.</p>\n<p>What animal is ideal in your situation.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 760629,
     "content_html": "Geese."
    },
    {
     "id": 760630,
     "content_html": "Pigs."
    },
    {
     "id": 760628,
     "content_html": "Sheep."
    },
    {
     "id": 760627,
     "content_html": "Cows."
    }
   ],
